  "summary_en": "UK Government white paper setting out a pro-innovation, context-based approach to AI regulation. Rather than new legislation, existing sector regulators apply five cross-cutting principles, supported by central coordination functions, risk monitoring, regulatory sandboxes and international standards engagement. Not specific to robotics or physical AI.",
  "key_provisions_or_claims": [
   "Five cross-sector principles: safety/security/robustness, transparency/explainability, fairness, accountability/governance, contestability/redress",
